{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"tool_name\":\"final\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"response\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"revise\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"work_item\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"20260908T113118\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The implementation substantially satisfies the deterministic-planning contract and all three required verification commands pass, but one bounded transactional identity defect remains: a successful named-school preflight is not committed to Deps when matching explicit IDs were also supplied.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"findings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"matching-explicit-and-resolved-identities-not-committed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"bounded\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"artifact\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"root1:execution/manual-phase0-continuation-2026-09-18.patch\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"requirement\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"acceptance/003-contract.yaml observable_behaviour.safe-transactional-school-resolution requires each named school's IDs to be staged in mention order, deduplicated without reordering, and committed to Deps after all mentions resolve; compatibility also requires directory preflights to remain observable.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"scenario\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"For a school-required question with both caller-supplied IDs and school_mentions that resolve to the same identities, plan_and_execute enters the identity_from_caller branch. After confirming equality, it sets deps.searched = True but does not append resolved_ids to deps.resolved_school_ids. The request also retains the caller-supplied ordering rather than using the staged mention ordering. Thus successful named resolution has occurred, yet its staged identity result is not committed as required.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"In the patch's transactional named-school resolution branch, the identity_from_caller path compares sorted(resolved_ids) with sorted(explicit_ids) and then only assigns deps.searched = True. The append loop and _attach_school_ids call exist solely in the else branch. The added tests cover conflicting explicit/resolved identities but do not cover the successful matching-explicit-plus-named scenario.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"required_revision\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"After all mentions resolve and matching explicit identities are confirmed, commit the staged ordered unique resolved IDs to deps.resolved_school_ids transactionally. Ensure the dispatched identity shape/order follows the contract's mention-order rule where applicable, and add a focused regression test for matching explicit and name-resolved identities. Preserve the existing no-mutation behavior on ambiguity, zero matches, malformed records, scalar multiplicity, and conflicts.\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"verified_evidence\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"artifact\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"root1:verification/001-full-test-suite.log\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"826 passed, 17 skipped, 5 deselected, 1 expected xfail; exit 0; no XPASS reported.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"artifact\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"root1:verification/002-affected-modules.log\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"172 affected-module tests passed; exit 0.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"artifact\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"root1:verification/003-focused-nonvacuous-acceptance.log\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"All 12 named acceptance nodes collected, expanding to 31 passing cases; exit 0.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"artifact\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"root2:methods/coding-harness/docs/phase-0-repairs/2026-09-first-manual-run/task-reports/06-independent-review-r2-provenance-2026-09-18.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The advisory review reports no high-priority blocker and confirms preserved product identities, but it is advisory rather than semantic authority and does not address the matching explicit-plus-resolved commit scenario.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"artifact\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"root1:observations/003-trust.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The operator explicitly accepted the historical hash-capture mismatch; it is not used as a reason for this revise outcome.\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"boundary_assessment\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The supplied diff otherwise stays within the five required product/test files and preserves the stated legacy-loop, evidence-contract, emitter, rendering, and Definition-Pack boundaries. No architectural or definition-authority decision is needed for the identified defect.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"authority_note\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"This semantic outcome does not authorize acceptance, merge, checkpoint closure, or work-item closure.\\\\\\\"}\\\"}\"}"}}
